;; /plan (byj-gly.360): a plan, written by agent$plan. A turn, as every
;; command that stands for an agent is (RFC-004): the session's agent hands
;; agent$plan the goal and what the conversation has established, and deals
;; with its three answers — a saved plan, one question (Need:), or a refusal
;; naming what should handle the request instead. The plan agent writes only
;; under .brainyard/plans/; nothing is built here.
;;
;; `/plan WORDS` plans what the words ask; `/plan` alone, the work the
;; conversation is about — with no turns yet the plan agent asks what it is.
;; Not in brainyard, which has no /plan command.
{:command "/plan"
 :agent "plan"
 :rephrase :predictor

 :default-request
 "Write a plan for the work this conversation is about."

 :purpose
 "write a plan — checked first for whether there is enough to plan, then saved under .brainyard/plans/ and graded — for what the words ask, or for the work the conversation is about"

 :usage
 "Call agent$plan with :question stating the goal in full: the request, and what this conversation has already established that the plan needs — decisions made, constraints, the files and commands involved — since the plan agent cannot see the conversation. Read its answer. `Saved plan:` — end with the plan's path, its approach and its grade as it gave them. `Need:` — when the conversation already answers its question, call agent$plan again with the answer added; otherwise end with its question, word for word, for the person to answer. `Refused:` — say why, and what it says should handle the request instead. Do not start carrying out the plan."

 :template
 "{request}

[{command}] This is {command}: {purpose}. {usage}"}
